"""Independent fixtures for exact requirement/control preparation binding."""
from argparse import ArgumentParser
from pathlib import Path
from builtins import ValueError, dict, list
import hashlib
import os
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile


def fail(message ∈ str) → None:
    raise ValueError(message)


def digest(path ∈ Path) → str:
    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def write_lines(path ∈ Path, lines ∈ list[str]) → None:
    joined ∈ str ← "\n".join(lines)
    path.write_text(joined + "\n")


def preparation(path ∈ Path, requirement_sha ∈ str) → None:
    write_lines(path, [
        "schema\tkitchen-a1-preparation-v1",
        "request_id\ta1-c67",
        "target\tphone",
        "device_instance\ta1-one",
        "operation\tdiagnostic-shizuku",
        "selected_action\tsource-test",
        "selected_status\tREADY",
        "selected_reason\tMATERIAL_BOUND",
        "requirement_projection_sha256\t" + requirement_sha,
        "action\tsource-test\tREADY\tMATERIAL_BOUND\ttemporary source test records its exact scope",
        "action\tfreshness-check\tREADY\tREAD_ONLY_REPEAT_ALLOWED\tcurrent facts are observed without mutation",
        "action\tdiagnostic-capture\tBLOCKED\tSHIZUKU_SERVICE_NOT_READY\tno diagnostic effect",
        "action\texport-copy\tBLOCKED\tSHIZUKU_EXPORT_MISSING\tno copy effect",
        "acceptance\tSOURCE_ONLY\tphysical identity authority service and device behavior remain unverified"
    ])


def selection(
    path ∈ Path,
    candidate ∈ Path,
    verifier ∈ Path,
    requirement_sha ∈ str,
    source_role ∈ str,
    destination_role ∈ str,
    omit_negative ∈ bool
) → None:
    lines ∈ list[str] ← [
        "schema\taici-requirement-control-selection-v1",
        "request_id\ta1-c67",
        "task\tsource-handoff",
        "target\tphone",
        "scope\tbaseline",
        "parameters_sha256\tbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb",
        "source_role\t" + source_role,
        "destination_role\t" + destination_role,
        "candidate_role\tcomplete-source-handoff-unit",
        "candidate_sha256\t" + digest(candidate),
        "requirement_projection_sha256\t" + requirement_sha,
        "verifier_owner\tisomorphisms/ai-ci",
        "verifier_revision\tcccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc",
        "verifier_sha256\t" + digest(verifier),
        "verifier_interface\taici-control-qualification-v1",
        "review_status\tapproved",
        "requirement\treq-exact-candidate\trequired\texact served bytes\tsource",
        "requirement\treq-live-effect\texcluded\tdownstream owner\tlive",
        "control\tcontrol-positive\treq-exact-candidate\tpositive\tPASS\tsource"
    ]
    if omit_negative == False:
        lines.append("control\tcontrol-negative\treq-exact-candidate\tnegative\tREJECTED\tfixture")
    write_lines(path, lines)


def evidence(
    path ∈ Path,
    directory ∈ Path,
    candidate ∈ Path,
    positive_execution ∈ str,
    positive_status ∈ str,
    scope ∈ str,
    omit_negative ∈ bool
) → None:
    stem ∈ str ← str(path.stem)
    positive ∈ Path ← directory.joinpath(stem + "-positive.txt")
    negative ∈ Path ← directory.joinpath(stem + "-negative.txt")
    positive.write_text("independent source control observed candidate bytes\n")
    negative.write_text("independent forged marker control rejected\n")
    lines ∈ list[str] ← [
        "schema\taici-executed-control-evidence-v1",
        "candidate_sha256\t" + digest(candidate),
        "parameters_sha256\tbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb",
        "target\tphone",
        "scope\t" + scope,
        "result\tcontrol-positive\treq-exact-candidate\t" + positive_execution + "\t" + positive_status + "\t" + digest(candidate) + "\tbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\tphone\tsource\t" + str(positive) + "\t" + digest(positive)
    ]
    if omit_negative == False:
        lines.append("result\tcontrol-negative\treq-exact-candidate\texecuted\tREJECTED\t" + digest(candidate) + "\tbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\tphone\tfixture\t" + str(negative) + "\t" + digest(negative))
    write_lines(path, lines)


def command(
    ithon ∈ str,
    qualifier ∈ Path,
    mode ∈ str,
    preparation_path ∈ Path,
    selection_path ∈ Path,
    evidence_path ∈ Path,
    candidate ∈ Path,
    verifier ∈ Path,
    output ∈ Path
) → list[str]:
    return [
        ithon, str(qualifier), mode,
        "--preparation", str(preparation_path),
        "--selection", str(selection_path),
        "--evidence", str(evidence_path),
        "--candidate", str(candidate),
        "--verifier", str(verifier),
        "--ithon", ithon,
        "--output", str(output)
    ]


def invoke(arguments ∈ list[str], cwd ∈ Path) → subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    environment ∈ dict[str, str] ← dict(os.environ)
    return subprocess.run(arguments, capture_output=True, cwd=str(cwd), env=environment)


def expect_pass(arguments ∈ list[str], cwd ∈ Path, label ∈ str) → subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    child ∈ subprocess.CompletedProcess ← invoke(arguments, cwd)
    code ∈ int ← child.returncode
    if code != 0:
        stderr ∈ str ← child.stderr.decode()
        fail(label + " unexpectedly failed: " + stderr)
    return child


def expect_reject(arguments ∈ list[str], cwd ∈ Path, diagnostic ∈ str, label ∈ str) → None:
    child ∈ subprocess.CompletedProcess ← invoke(arguments, cwd)
    code ∈ int ← child.returncode
    if code == 0:
        fail(label + " unexpectedly passed")
    stderr ∈ str ← child.stderr.decode()
    diagnostic_index ∈ int ← stderr.find(diagnostic)
    if diagnostic_index < 0:
        fail(label + " wrong diagnostic: " + stderr)


def case_files(
    directory ∈ Path,
    name ∈ str,
    candidate ∈ Path,
    verifier ∈ Path,
    requirement_sha ∈ str,
    source_role ∈ str,
    destination_role ∈ str,
    omit_negative ∈ bool,
    positive_execution ∈ str,
    positive_status ∈ str,
    scope ∈ str
) → tuple[Path, Path]:
    selected ∈ Path ← directory.joinpath(name + "-selection.tsv")
    observed ∈ Path ← directory.joinpath(name + "-evidence.tsv")
    selection(selected, candidate, verifier, requirement_sha, source_role, destination_role, omit_negative)
    evidence(observed, directory, candidate, positive_execution, positive_status, scope, omit_negative)
    return (selected, observed)


def main() → None:
    parser ∈ ArgumentParser ← ArgumentParser()
    parser.add_argument("--ithon", required=True)
    args ∈ object ← parser.parse_args()
    ithon ∈ str ← args.ithon
    source_name ∈ str ← sys._getframe().f_code.co_filename
    root ∈ Path ← Path(source_name).resolve().parents.__getitem__(1)
    qualifier ∈ Path ← root.joinpath("tasks/source-handoff/qualify.pi")
    verifier ∈ Path ← root.joinpath("tests/fixtures/source-handoff-qualification/aici-verifier.pi")
    temporary_name ∈ str ← tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="kitchen qualification ")
    temporary ∈ Path ← Path(temporary_name)
    outside ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("unrelated whitespace")
    outside.mkdir()
    checked ∈ int ← 0
    requirement_sha ∈ str ← "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
    try:
        prepared ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("preparation.tsv")
        preparation(prepared, requirement_sha)
        candidate ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("served candidate")
        write_lines(candidate, [
            "candidate diagnostic text: PASS strings do not qualify controls",
            "if sh /absolute/source-handoff/2.sh run; then true; fi",
            "# source-handoff-unit=COMPLETE"
        ])
        good_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "good", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        good_selection ∈ Path ← good_paths.__getitem__(0)
        good_evidence ∈ Path ← good_paths.__getitem__(1)
        good_output ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("qualified.tsv")
        good_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, good_selection,
            good_evidence, candidate, verifier, good_output
        )
        expect_pass(good_command, outside, "exact candidate and controls")
        verify_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "verify", prepared, good_selection,
            good_evidence, candidate, verifier, good_output
        )
        expect_pass(verify_command, outside, "unchanged qualified preparation")
        checked ← checked + 2

        equal_output ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("qualified-equal.tsv")
        equal_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, good_selection,
            good_evidence, candidate, verifier, equal_output
        )
        expect_pass(equal_command, outside, "deterministic repeat")
        good_bytes ∈ bytes ← good_output.read_bytes()
        equal_bytes ∈ bytes ← equal_output.read_bytes()
        if good_bytes != equal_bytes:
            fail("equal material changed qualified preparation")
        checked ← checked + 1

        served_b ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("served-b")
        candidate_bytes ∈ bytes ← candidate.read_bytes()
        served_b.write_bytes(candidate_bytes + b"# rewrite\n")
        served_b_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, good_selection,
            good_evidence, served_b, verifier, temporary.joinpath("served-b.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(served_b_command, outside, "SERVED_CANDIDATE_CHANGED", "tested A served B")
        checked ← checked + 1

        omitted_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "omitted", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", True, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        omitted_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, omitted_paths.__getitem__(0),
            omitted_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("omitted.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(omitted_command, outside, "lacks positive or negative control", "omitted negative control")
        checked ← checked + 1

        unexecuted_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "unexecuted", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "not-run", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        unexecuted_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, unexecuted_paths.__getitem__(0),
            unexecuted_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("unexecuted.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(unexecuted_command, outside, "selected control was not executed", "unexecuted control")
        checked ← checked + 1

        role_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "wrong-role", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "move", "copy", False, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        role_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, role_paths.__getitem__(0),
            role_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("wrong-role.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(role_command, outside, "wrong copy or move role", "wrong copy move roles")
        checked ← checked + 1

        stale_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "stale", candidate, verifier, "dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd",
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        stale_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, stale_paths.__getitem__(0),
            stale_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("stale.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(stale_command, outside, "SELECTION_REQUIREMENTS_CHANGED", "stale correction")
        checked ← checked + 1

        scope_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "scope", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "PASS", "repaired-feature"
        )
        scope_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, scope_paths.__getitem__(0),
            scope_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("scope.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(scope_command, outside, "evidence binding changed scope", "wrong scope")
        checked ← checked + 1

        refuse_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "always-refuse", candidate, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "REJECTED", "baseline"
        )
        refuse_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, refuse_paths.__getitem__(0),
            refuse_paths.__getitem__(1), candidate, verifier, temporary.joinpath("always-refuse.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(refuse_command, outside, "result differs from required observation", "always refusing candidate")
        checked ← checked + 1

        formatted ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("served candidate formatted")
        write_lines(formatted, [
            "candidate diagnostic text: PASS strings do not qualify controls",
            "",
            "if sh /absolute/source-handoff/2.sh run; then true; fi",
            "# harmless formatting changed and qualification reran",
            "# source-handoff-unit=COMPLETE"
        ])
        formatted_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "formatted", formatted, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        formatted_output ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("formatted-qualified.tsv")
        formatted_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, formatted_paths.__getitem__(0),
            formatted_paths.__getitem__(1), formatted, verifier, formatted_output
        )
        expect_pass(formatted_command, outside, "newly qualified formatting change")
        formatted_bytes ∈ bytes ← formatted_output.read_bytes()
        original_bytes ∈ bytes ← good_output.read_bytes()
        if formatted_bytes == original_bytes:
            fail("changed candidate retained old qualification bytes")
        checked ← checked + 1

        incomplete ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("incomplete candidate")
        incomplete.write_text("partial source-handoff bytes\n")
        incomplete_paths ∈ tuple[Path, Path] ← case_files(
            temporary, "incomplete", incomplete, verifier, requirement_sha,
            "copy", "move", False, "executed", "PASS", "baseline"
        )
        incomplete_command ∈ list[str] ← command(
            ithon, qualifier, "prepare", prepared, incomplete_paths.__getitem__(0),
            incomplete_paths.__getitem__(1), incomplete, verifier, temporary.joinpath("incomplete.tsv")
        )
        expect_reject(incomplete_command, outside, "SERVED_CANDIDATE_INCOMPLETE", "incomplete served unit")
        checked ← checked + 1

        positive_file ∈ Path ← temporary.joinpath("good-evidence-positive.txt")
        positive_file.write_text("changed after qualification\n")
        expect_reject(verify_command, outside, "result evidence bytes changed", "changed executed evidence")
        checked ← checked + 1
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(temporary_name)
    print("PASS", checked, "exact requirement/control qualification cases")


main()
